to new ideas and being a show\u2011off could impair crew cooperation, which is also safety-critical. So we can argue that B's interpersonal issues (grumpy, uncooperative) are also concerns, but perhaps less severe than C's rigidity.\n\nWe need to reference explicit facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also B can be grumpy and uncooperative. C can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but not open to new ideas, not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized, regarded as a show\u2011off.\n\nWe can argue that C's inability to accept feedback could be a bigger risk than B's grumpiness, especially for long flights where crew coordination is vital. Also C's unorganized nature could affect attention to detail. So we might keep B.\n\nThus we will keep vote for Candidate B, stating reasons.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
